  "body": "### Summary\nThe LOT-114 tests merged in #464 (fad1d70) fail at random in \"App build + tests (iOS 27 simulator)\", so CI goes red on PRs that do not touch the filter view. The failures look like timing problems: each failing test ends after exactly 60 s, while the neighbouring FilteredPosts tests take 80 s on the same parallel clone.\n\n### Evidence\n- #463 (head 0dd767a, job 127270112957): `FilteredPostsEntryTests.aRowWithoutAResumeLinkStartsAtItsOwnPage()` failed.\n- #466 (head daa0f28, job 127279363058): `FilteredPostsModelTests.aRunCancelledWhileItsBatchIsBeingNormalizedNeverDelivers()` failed after exactly 60.000 s.\n- dev-swift itself was green at fad1d70 and at 8b431fb. Both jobs were re-run.\n\n### Scope\n- Make the FilteredPosts app tests deterministic. Wait on explicit signals (continuations or gated doubles) instead of `settle` timing or wall-clock limits. A limit, where one is still needed, must be generous and reached only on a real hang. LESSONS: see #366 / #385 for the \"fail fast instead of a wall-clock limit\" pattern.\n- Tests only, unless a real race in `FilteredPostsModel` shows up. In that case, fix it and say so.\n\n### Acceptance\n- The FilteredPosts suites pass 3 times in a row on CI.\n- No test depends on wall-clock time for its verdict.\n\n/claim cloud/fix-filter-tests",
